<title>USA: Bioject to sell products in Wal-Mart.</title>
<headline>Bioject to sell products in Wal-Mart.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bioject Medical Technologies Inc on Wednesday said about 400 of Wal-Mart Stores Inc's retail outlets will offer customers flu vaccines using the Biojector 2000 needle-free injection system in WalMart's national flu program this fall.</p>
<p>Financial details were undisclosed.</p>
<p>The Biojector 2000 uses jet injection technology to deliver medication through a small opening about one-third the size of the smallest needle, in a disposable, plastic needle-free syringe.</p>
</text>
